# Kocevski et al. (2025), ApJ 986, 126: "The Rise of Faint, Red AGN at z>4: A Sample of Little Red Dots in the JWST Extragalactic Legacy Fields"
# arXiv:2404.03576v3 (accepted version), Table 4 (rest-frame UV LF of LRDs); identical to Table 4 of the published article
# Redshift: 6.5 < z < 8.5 (file at the bin centre z = 7.5)
# Magnitude definition: M1450 = blue (rest-UV) power-law continuum fit extrapolated to rest-frame 1450 A; observed total UV light,
#   no dust correction and no host/AGN decomposition (the paper argues the rest-UV of LRDs is host-dominated)
# Phi convention: log10(Phi / Mpc^-3 mag^-1), 1-mag bins, asymmetric errors in dex (Gehrels 1986 Poisson); H0=70, Om=0.3, OL=0.7
# Note: Photometrically selected LRDs (CEERS, PRIMER-COSMOS, PRIMER-UDS, JADES, NGDEEP); UNCOVER sources excluded from the LF.
# Note: 1/Vmax estimator; symmetric errors (+/-) are repeated in both columns. The M1450=-22 bin contains a single object.
#
# M1450  LogPhi  UpperDeltaDex  LowerDeltaDex
